                            <h3>Introduction</h3>
                            <p><p align="justify">The Fabric and Apparel Design (FYUP) is offered in ODL mode that integrates textile science, fashion design, and apparel manufacturing. The programme is designed to provide students with a strong foundation in fabric production, garment construction, surface design, and apparel development, while also fostering creativity, technical competence, and industry-oriented skills. This programme provides professional excellence in the fashion and textiles industry as designers, product developers, merchandisers, entrepreneurs, educators, and researchers.</p></p>
                            <h3>Objective</h3>
                            <p><ol><li>The programme aims to provide students with a comprehensive understanding of the fabric and apparel manufacturing industry.</li>
 <li>The programme intends to equip students with the technical knowledge and skills necessary for fabric and apparel production.</li>
 <li>The programme seeks to develop students' expertise in manufacturing processes specific to the fabric and apparel industry and provide successful careers in fabric and apparel production.</li></ol>
 </p>
